{"step_index":7034,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-25T14:19:15Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-25T14:19:15Z\nCompleted At: 2026-09-25T14:19:19Z\nThe search for \"\"iam.managed.disableServiceAccountKeyCreation\" \"DENY\" override edit\" returned the following summary:\nTo manage the **`iam.managed.disableServiceAccountKeyCreation`** organization policy constraint, you must have the **Organization Policy Administrator** role (`roles/orgpolicy.policyAdmin`) at the organization level[1][2][3].\n\nIf you are blocked by this policy, here is the standard process to override it for a specific project or the entire organization[1][3]:\n\n### 1. Verify Your Permissions\n*   You must be assigned the **Organization Policy Administrator** role at the **organization level**[2][3]. \n*   This role often does not appear in the role list for individual projects; you must select your organization in the resource picker (top-left of the Google Cloud Console) to grant or verify this role[4][2][3].\n\n### 2. Override the Policy\nOnce you have the required permissions, you can modify the policy at the project or organization level[3]:\n1.  Go to the **[Organization Policies](https://console.cloud.google.com/iam-admin/orgpolicies)** page in the Google Cloud Console[5][3].\n2.  Use the filter to search for **`iam.managed.disableServiceAccountKeyCreation`**[1][3].\n3.  Click on the policy name to open its details[1][3].\n4.  Click **Manage policy**[1][3].\n5.  Select **Override parent's policy** (this is critical if the policy is being inherited from the organization)[6][7][3].\n6.  Under **Enforcement**, select **Off** (or \"Not enforced\")[8][5][3].\n7.  Click **Set policy**[8][3].\n\n### Important Troubleshooting Notes\n*   **Dual Constraints:** Google Cloud often utilizes both a legacy constraint (`iam.disableServiceAccountKeyCreation`) and a managed constraint (`iam.managed.disableServiceAccountKeyCreation`)[1][9]. If you disable one but the block persists, ensure you have checked and overridden **both**[1][9].\n*   **Propagation Time:** Changes to organization policies are not always instantaneous and may take a few minutes to propagat\n<truncated 1547 bytes>\ng-api-redirect/AUZIYQGrZawelSUvc5L0peJLl4U72miZfffj5rJ-lBUCktXyvtwLVRgKmtctyq_cBOoBH0LgpF6vonGYdbh68qng7kN6VFGfsQZYzE4qQNCQbOdHKNd9OhnZGBYyCXN-3GGmDTc4NQwpr-mMsNG79z6yEFK__Byyl14MdV5JErNQLiVj0pEYLNKcPSn3ZVlD5B-obVLdWqA=)\n[6] [reddit.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHtPTKdiU9QN_81tFQmk9NoXW7BIQ4wJydhnqUZqn1KzjCUloDdmcxjTqDB5Br8A_1dGw8H9_Ifx8YBlPMdEwul3SAuXsdT8Zl2F5HWBtkrRn-ZFfIjAQWYvB9jlRD8mQAu8D_bmQQaUhurmY9T9b6DLEXcKU-aSTE7dT42WAm_bg-2nCGhKb8NKE2CAfY4NYkyeElZ5u9T17emhazm)\n[7] [reddit.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHtPTKdiU9QN_81tFQmk9NoXW7BIQ4wJydhnqUZqn1KzjCUloDdmcxjTqDB5Br8A_1dGw8H9_Ifx8YBlPMdEwul3SAuXsdT8Zl2F5HWBtkrRn-ZFfIjAQWYvB9jlRD8mQAu8D_bmQQaUhurmY9T9b6DLEXcKU-aSTE7dT42WAm_bg-2nCGhKb8NKE2CAfY4NYkyeElZ5u9T17emhazm)\n[8] [google.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHL_vGKJyQv_nZaP1L_TO_Gf4oKx0taM9-thxWJlQueeJsjTHv24q7NPQJat49u-9ZD4eNbDMaVpmUWiJemGOiZ4KeKyKFaUl7xIbBwr9xMZKu1udynDk19mXyJ7ZZQ8AbRBBUldkdGpYo0cUmq8QyONorFH8i3_tyOZbpNYBdqc4o=)\n[9] [dev.to](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHCi-QZhmzCGe5zvtBQBMjQdUAldP59xuS9R3AmX7ytTbWEgKUX_CZgxnQw6H9MdhTJaOYg0aLSdZkmtgDFN04ggeGOWJiM6XbO11sIFR3gK6efrjSHZ2yV2oG6uAGD0NoRNgUefSsjF0_vsobEg2iF_rOqBt1vd0GnXzTXO0IlXTM-tH69-lkcxoElkl_idw7oWM7j2AZiBB40Df57)\n[10] [techwithtyler.dev](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH_KyDw8REI0Kbb4HhNESDrWvWgdec5NTHb_8kLwoI-U-htHHQbJZqtvipMiQD0Y_7EbMaSxF-SRVMT-CCU6teA3XpRQ1nguJW2UcRpr5hb5-SelzLqZVRvWF6Eyh_roYZWBfejjAloyIYhqFVzkTvZbrpcDH_lpWE7yPGXFMdtdeBplgKKWV09kWx5hvGRg77K7CXnl71F78BlVB2OhF55V-ENP-ULsMEXjDMDkQWJpZbN)\n[11] [oneuptime.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/groun