{"step_index":7036,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-25T14:19:24Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-25T14:19:24Z\nCompleted At: 2026-09-25T14:19:28Z\nThe search for \"\"iam.managed.disableServiceAccountKeyCreation\" \"secure by default\" opt out or disable\" returned the following summary:\nThe organization policy `iam.managed.disableServiceAccountKeyCreation` is part of Google Cloud's **\"secure-by-default\"** baseline, which is automatically enforced for all organizations created on or after May 3, 2024[1][2][3].\n\nThis policy is designed to improve security by preventing the creation of long-lived, user-managed service account keys, which are a common vector for security compromises[4][5][6].\n\n### Can you opt out or disable it?\nYes, you can disable or override this policy, but it requires specific administrative privileges[7][8]. Because it is an organization-level policy, you cannot override it if you only have project-level permissions[9][10].\n\n### How to Disable or Modify the Policy\nTo modify this constraint, you must have the **Organization Policy Administrator** (`roles/orgpolicy.policyAdmin`) or **Organization Administrator** (`roles/resourcemanager.organizationAdmin`) role[7][10][8].\n\n1.  **Navigate to Organization Policies:** Go to the Google Cloud Console, select your organization, and navigate to **IAM & Admin > Organization policies**[10][8].\n2.  **Locate the Constraint:** Search for `iam.managed.disableServiceAccountKeyCreation`[10][8].\n3.  **Manage/Edit Policy:** Click on the policy name. If it is enforced at the organization level, you can choose to:\n    *   **Disable it:** Change the enforcement state to \"Off\" (or \"Not enforced\")[8].\n    *   **Create an Exception:** Depending on your needs, you may be able to set the policy to apply only to specific projects or folders rather than the entire organization[6][10].\n\n### Important Considerations\n*   **Legacy vs. Managed Constraints:** Google is transitioning from legacy policies (e.g., `iam.disableServiceAccountKeyCreation`) to managed versions (`iam.managed.disableServiceAccountKeyCreation`)[11][10]. If you are still blocked after modifyi\n<truncated 1909 bytes>\nirect/AUZIYQFYcMXZHWPE6tfu2LQ8Kbtfex_eT3N00u7Nog6rWCJeBKQqt1oLgAFulzg75CCdGqYp6G3NJoBToMV0wHfc9nPjjUsUBs_3BwsEcxrcmXdRGWWaORlgvNeV3r4Snqa3OwN0SsAz0UTl-kM0pUCUggb--3QpBD1hy_z99nUj16G5d03PuHM_yCmlXIKlP7RsYRNh_KjqgRHbQLlFZHhZZDrqNDr4auLzMb5yA3_yAncW6GdyJcCx80SviFZ-boTqrSlx)\n[7] [google.dev](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQF6Vme56nKnicRtVQeNtkKbOf9TZ-f4-2x0oX7_HaqD0QpJFkKZmrc0FCo9sj86avavpLOG9sB4bJSSWa4nxKTw5dr-nD62cNyd_-1DbkGXNV0XPEu5kYjPHIRUSpMJBWGFph_ObJB4xhbM1lo1teuNdWkPcCoEyzc9f9NkoAHWH5VPDZ0_5VJXzP7SY--mPieOhEtf0ODiMEd_nuWJGe_7piSUQzZzC0b-2FfYqnstY941Y0MNSiNAo9jTrw==)\n[8] [subsplash.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFTjW1ue46U6yPYQp3ztVGVbVCkcDoKc_TZ0twLfIVKrLK_GSc3hccnPACGY8xKBEt6Od3EiYtVeD85BNdho3kittvx2MWDXOLMXsssNfbN5EWyMrNpBBgkNA8jNR2pMhifXALVpu-jGFTUb88z2eq-tMKr4_cvAk4iGI_LImDjerY9T-DuXtEMLqdjKbwSsK1-reUMxi4jpXXZefEeosF5D7n_fUxCaV2Lgc_WINk=)\n[9] [google.dev](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQF6Vme56nKnicRtVQeNtkKbOf9TZ-f4-2x0oX7_HaqD0QpJFkKZmrc0FCo9sj86avavpLOG9sB4bJSSWa4nxKTw5dr-nD62cNyd_-1DbkGXNV0XPEu5kYjPHIRUSpMJBWGFph_ObJB4xhbM1lo1teuNdWkPcCoEyzc9f9NkoAHWH5VPDZ0_5VJXzP7SY--mPieOhEtf0ODiMEd_nuWJGe_7piSUQzZzC0b-2FfYqnstY941Y0MNSiNAo9jTrw==)\n[10] [dev.to](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEblIqgDjFfhg3rrridfPlAg-lmEuO9sSkMxqqnnTTTB-xVh4ijvkOFDfadvtw8VLlbrQsaG5isqiGEZNLrDjLHznW1AS0il4biyYcN_s-jaoSivNAkkdpZ3FkhNdEfHola5faGzfS5bpzgXE6oJJ8gYQJ69bkU_Xi9B30FjMM5MdNfftl1XzyfKDaKAFk62n-YQFPLgvpx7wJ7dD8=)\n[11] [digitalden.cloud](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFJd9EQJVS9LkERAK8x5KwjsMsERLiJpt5vjmer6-yy-t8Zw5DgwQhjBgoEJ7w9Yst_KSzJnhesuCFM_oEX8InYBVjCbtuI-d32J03mA-